LICENSE PLACEHOLDER
===================

This repository does not yet have a license applied.

The repository owner has not yet chosen a license. Until a license is added,
default copyright law applies: no one other than the copyright holder has
the right to reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works from this
software.

Before publishing this repository publicly, the owner should:

1. Choose a license appropriate for an open-source news aggregator. Common
   choices include:
   - MIT — permissive, minimal restrictions.
   - Apache-2.0 — permissive, includes an explicit patent grant.
   - AGPL-3.0 — copyleft; notably requires that anyone who runs a modified
     version of this software as a network service (e.g. a competing
     hosted instance) must also make their modified source available. This
     is a common choice for self-hostable web applications that the author
     wants to keep open even when run as a service.
   - GPL-3.0 — copyleft, but (unlike AGPL) does not cover the
     network-use case.
2. Replace this file's contents with the full text of the chosen license.
3. Update the `license` field in `package.json`.
4. Update the badge/section in `README.md` that currently points here.
5. Add a short SPDX identifier comment (e.g. `// SPDX-License-Identifier:
   MIT`) to source files if the chosen license's community conventions
   expect one.

This is the one part of the project the repository owner asked to handle
personally — everything else here is ready to publish.
